{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":498597,"name":"Roberto De la Fuente","username":"rdelafuente","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/rdelafuente/{size}/121824_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-22T22:52:54.444Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor IDE\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn a long-lived My Machines worker started from the terminal (systemd service, not IDE Remote Control), Cloud Agent runs often enter a claim/detach loop:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorker claims the agent (\u003ccode\u003eWorker claimed by background composer\u003c/code\u003e, Agent Store opens).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShortly after, the claim closes with \u003ccode\u003ecancelReason\u003c/code\u003e / reason \u003ccode\u003econtroller_disconnected\u003c/code\u003e (\u003ccode\u003eClosed Agent Store claim after controller detach\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe same \u003ccode\u003ebcId\u003c/code\u003e is claimed again (sometimes multiple overlapping claims within seconds).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBridge heartbeats continue; the worker process stays up (no crash, no OOM, no sleep, no \u003ccode\u003e--idle-release-timeout\u003c/code\u003e exit). Auth token refresh reconnects in under a second when it happens.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach detach appears to reset Agent Store / session attachment mid-exploration. The model then re-orients (re-lists tree, re-reads rules, rediscovers tools, resumes checklists) instead of continuing the task. For a trivial one-file null-guard this has stretched a run to many hours with little useful progress until an external interrupt forced commit/PR.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis matches the pattern in \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/terminal-started-my-machines-worker-repeatedly-disconnects-while-runs-continue/168770\"\u003eTerminal-started My Machines worker repeatedly disconnects while runs continue\u003c/a\u003e: healthy worker + bridge, loop is on the controller attach path, not “machine went offline.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-environment-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-environment-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eEnvironment\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOS: Linux (dedicated always-on box)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorker: My Machines, terminal/\u003ccode\u003eagent worker start\u003c/code\u003e under systemd (single named worker; not intentionally running a parallel IDE-managed worker on the same roots)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePrivacy Mode: enabled\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAgent CLI: current stable at time of observation (can provide exact version on request)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRepos: multiple \u003ccode\u003e--worker-dir\u003c/code\u003e checkouts on the same machine\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-steps-to-reproduce-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-steps-to-reproduce-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart a named My Machines worker from the terminal and keep it running.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLaunch a Cloud Agent targeted at that worker on a real multi-file repo (git discovery / explore phase matters).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGive a small coding task (e.g. null-safe access in one helper).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWatch worker logs during early exploration (branch/worktree discovery, reads).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-expected-behavior-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-expected-behavior-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne stable claim for the agent until the run finishes or the user cancels. Controller detach should not flap. The model should keep task state across tool calls without re-booting orientation every few minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-actual-behavior-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-actual-behavior-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eActual Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRepeated \u003ccode\u003econtroller_disconnected\u003c/code\u003e → close claim → reclaim same \u003ccode\u003ebcId\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOccasional burst of multiple claims for one agent in ~20s\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAgent Store reset mid-run → model thrash / “lost thread”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorker process and bridge remain healthy\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTrivial fixes become non-viable on self-hosted vs the same change in a local Cursor Agent session on a developer machine\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-log-pattern-redacted-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-log-pattern-redacted-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eLog pattern (redacted)\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eINFO Worker claimed by background composer\n  bcId=\"bc-…\"\n  agentStoreRequested=true\n  agentStoreActive=true\nINFO Closed Agent Store claim after controller detach\n  bcId=\"bc-…\"\n  reason=\"controller_disconnected\"\nINFO Worker claimed by background composer\n  bcId=\"bc-…\"   # same id; sometimes logged multiple times in a short window\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBridge heartbeat frames continue (~30s) across the flap. No transport/auth failure in the worker log around those events (aside from routine token refresh).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-notes-for-eng-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-notes-for-eng-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eNotes for eng\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlease treat this as the controller/session-attachment class (as in the Aug 2026 thread), not classic “Worker Disconnected / machine asleep.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFlapping is most damaging during explore/git discovery, when Agent Store reset forces full re-orientation.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHappy to share redacted \u003ccode\u003ebcId\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003erunId\u003c/code\u003e pairs and a longer log slice privately if useful.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-operating-system-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-operating-system-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-version-information-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-version-information-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIDE: \u003ccode\u003e3.20.21\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nCLI Version: \u003ccode\u003e2026.09.02-c22c1a3\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot: \u003ccode\u003e0.57.1\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-additional-information-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-additional-information-11\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis issue stops me from using Cursor self-hosted Cloud Agents on non-trivial or even trivial autofix workloads. Local Agent in the IDE remains usable; self-hosted is not reliable enough for unattended runs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate: Since filing, upgraded the worker CLI to \u003ccode\u003e2026.09.18-9a7762b\u003c/code\u003e; will report back if the claim/detach loop still occurs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498597-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-12\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498597-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-12\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-22T22:59:29.092Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":25.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":172713,"topic_slug":"my-machines-worker-repeated-controller-disconnected-claim-detach-resets-agent-store-mid-run-model-thrash-lost-thread","display_username":"Roberto De la Fuente","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/terminal-started-my-machines-worker-repeatedly-disconnects-while-runs-continue/168770","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Terminal-started My Machines worker repeatedly disconnects while runs continue","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139310,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/my-machines-worker-repeated-controller-disconnected-claim-detach-resets-agent-store-mid-run-model-thrash-lost-thread/172713/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false}],"stream":[